1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,306
Dijkstra's algorithm finds the shortest distance from one start node

2
00:00:04,406 --> 00:00:07,832
to every other node. The numbers on the edges are lengths.

3
00:00:07,932 --> 00:00:09,773
Every length must be zero or more.

4
00:00:09,866 --> 00:00:12,164
At the start, A has distance zero.

5
00:00:12,264 --> 00:00:16,640
Every other node has distance infinity. Then repeat two steps.

6
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:20,297
First, settle the unsettled node with the smallest distance.

7
00:00:20,397 --> 00:00:21,872
Second, update its neighbors:

8
00:00:21,972 --> 00:00:24,969
if a path through it is shorter, keep the shorter distance.

9
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:29,170
Settle A. From A, B is four away, and C is two away.

10
00:00:29,266 --> 00:00:33,109
The smallest estimate is now C, at two. Settle C.

11
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:35,571
Through C, B is two plus one: three.

12
00:00:35,671 --> 00:00:38,417
That is shorter than four, so B becomes three.

13
00:00:38,517 --> 00:00:41,054
D becomes ten, and E becomes twelve.

14
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:45,462
Settle B, at three. Through B, D is three plus five: eight.

15
00:00:45,562 --> 00:00:46,870
Eight is shorter than ten.

16
00:00:46,966 --> 00:00:51,304
Settle D, at eight. E becomes ten, and F becomes fourteen.

17
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,346
Pause here and predict. D is settled.

18
00:00:54,446 --> 00:00:56,970
Which node is settled next, and at what distance?

19
00:01:00,066 --> 00:01:03,888
E, at ten. It is the smallest unsettled estimate.

20
00:01:03,988 --> 00:01:05,765
Through E, F becomes thirteen.

21
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:08,916
Settle F, at thirteen. Every node is settled.

22
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,106
Why is a settled distance final?

23
00:01:11,206 --> 00:01:15,338
Any other path must leave the settled nodes through an unsettled node,

24
00:01:15,438 --> 00:01:17,365
which is already at least as far.

25
00:01:17,465 --> 00:01:20,696
With no negative lengths, the rest of that path cannot make it

26
00:01:20,796 --> 00:01:21,120
shorter.

27
00:01:21,216 --> 00:01:25,370
The edges that gave each final distance form the shortest-path tree.

28
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:30,094
The shortest path to F is A, C, B, D, E, F. Its length is thirteen.
